    {
      "id": "claim_316a9f98e07f4b3c91d739421475bb52",
      "statement": "A session poisoned by a failed storage commit is unrecoverable in-process, so Supervisor.Call restarts the sidecar once and retries; Restart drops the connection before killing the process and zeroes the crash counter because a deliberate restart is not a crash.",
      "evidence": [
